From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:19:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 079/106] render: puppet blend shapes (MDMP), their weight
 tracks and bone alpha
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Decoded from wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485's MDL loader (GH 0x1402873f0) and the stock genericimage4
(MORPHING, SKINNING_ALPHA) and 2.8.485's base/morph_vertex_v1.h:

- MDMP0001: per mesh a u16 target count; with targets the f32 position scale and the u32 point
  count N; per target a u64 id, a name, N · 6 bytes of snorm16 xyz (value / 32767, at least −1,
  × the scale), then by the mesh's flags N · 6 normal bytes (0x400), N · 2 alpha bytes (0x1000)
  and a bone rule (0x2000: u32, u32, f32, f32; parsed, not applied). A vertex's point is its vec4
  position's w − 1 (format 0x10000; 0 = none).
- MDLA v4 blend-shape weights: per mesh flags (bit 0), a float (the scale again), a u16 count,
  then per track the target's index and frames + 1 floats. MDLA v3's bone alpha tracks (a flag
  byte, then per bone a u32 and frames + 1 floats) are read too. MDLE0002 is a byte count and a
  copy of the bones' local matrices (not used).
- Applied as genericimage4 does: the morph before the skin (position + Σ weight · delta), the
  vertex alpha Π (alpha · w + 1 − w) × saturate (Σ weight · bone alpha).
- IImageLayer getBlendShapeIndex / getBlendShapeWeight / setBlendShapeWeight (by name or index,
  every mesh's targets in order). A set weight holds over the animations'.

Inferred: how the layers mix these (as the position: normal lerps from 0, additive adds; bone
alpha from 1). Ours: LWE poses puppets on the CPU, so the vertex alpha reaches genericimage4's
fragment through its VERTEXCOLOR (a_Color = 1 1 1 alpha, multiplied right after WE's
v_VertexAlpha); genericimage2 has neither, in WE too. 3490034653's 人物1 blinks with its one
target ("眨眼", 25 eyelid points); its alphas are all 1.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md F3 (blend shapes, bone alpha)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
